      "claim": "Nifedipine has an absolute oral bioavailability of 0.43 ± 0.14 in humans, which is above the 20% threshold, but this small dihydropyridine is structurally and physicochemically distant from the large lipophilic polyprenyl quinone query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C35"],
      "claim": "Isradipine has a mean systemic availability of about 16.5% in healthy volunteers, below the 20% threshold, but its low bioavailability is mainly due to first-pass metabolism rather than the poor solubility/absorption expected for the query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C28"],
      "claim": "Pentazocine has an oral bioavailability of about 18% in normal subjects, below the 20% threshold, but it is a small opioid analgesic and not structurally related to the ubiquinone query.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C17"],
      "claim": "Rigosertib has an absolute oral bioavailability of 34.8% in fasting patients, above the threshold, but this is formulation- and condition-dependent and does not transfer to the highly lipophilic, poorly soluble CoQ10-like query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C16"],
      "claim": "Soraprazan has an oral bioavailability of 50% in healthy volunteers, above the threshold, but it is a small soluble drug and not a relevant structural or physicochemical analogue of the query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The query is recognized as ubiquinone-10 (CoQ10), a large, highly lipophilic polyprenyl benzoquinone with established poor oral bioavailability. The experimental records are mostly small drug-like molecules with low transferability; the query-specific physicochemical and known absorption behavior support F below 20%.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental oral bioavailability record for the query molecule itself is provided.",
    "No structurally close polyprenyl quinone analogue with measured absolute oral bioavailability is present among the evidence records.",
    "The available records do not address the effect of formulation, food, or solubilization on the query's absorption."
